* '''Comment''' I have largely tried to stay of this dispute until it reaches some kind of resolution that can be implemented, and I think we are approaching that stage with DWB's suggestions:
**Proposal 1: {{quote|''"The Birth of a Nation is a 1915 American silent epic drama film directed by D. W. Griffith. Adapted from Thomas Dixon Jr.’s 1905 novel and play, The Clansman, the film was co-written by Griffith and Frank E. Woods. It is widely considered a landmark in the development of cinematic technique, noted for its innovative use of camera shots and editing. The film's narrative depicts the American Civil War and Reconstruction era, portraying the Ku Klux Klan as a heroic force. Its release was met with significant controversy due to its highly criticized racial themes."''}}
**Proposal 2: {{quote|''"The Birth of a Nation, a 1915 American silent epic drama, was directed by D. W. Griffith and starred Lillian Gish. The film is an adaptation of Thomas Dixon Jr.'s novel and play, The Clansman: A Historical Romance of the Ku Klux Klan. Historically, it is recognized for its pioneering contributions to cinematic language and technique, influencing future filmmakers with its use of sophisticated camera and editing methods. However, the film is also one of the most controversial in American history due to its overtly racist content, which includes demeaning portrayals of African Americans and a positive depiction of the Ku Klux Klan."'' }}
:I am fine with both of them, but the second is more frank and therefore probably better. I still object to characterising the film as "white supremacist propaganda", because this gives too much prominence to a minority label. I do not have an issue with highlighting its white supremacist themes, and incidentally it was me who  [https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=The_Birth_of_a_Nation&diff=prev&oldid=1260841731 introduced that into the article]. I completely dispute the fact that the [[WP:WEIGHT]]] of sources is behind describing it as "propaganda". While I accept it was a propaganda tool for KKK, that was not its purpose for creation and is not reflected in the majority of sources. I would like to get more thoughts on the wording proposed by DWB. Once we agree on the wording here we can then implement it in the main article. [[User:Betty Logan|Betty Logan]] ([[User talk:Betty Logan|talk]]) 23:38, 15 August 2025 (UTC)

